{"slug": "gemini-4-argon", "names": ["Gemini 4 Argon"], "data": {"data": [{"author_id": "2109582849560985600", "created_at": "2026-10-14T04:00:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2110219196907090012"], "id": "2110219196907090012", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1923572500719693824", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2110214698696409548", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Umesh__digital Gemini 4 Argon is incredible for building personal projects. Its deep reasoning capabilities and massive context window make refactoring code, debugging, and shipping full-stack apps much faster. \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f\ud83d\udd25", "url": "https://x.com/ussman174/status/2110219196907090012"}, {"author_id": "2043712650886942721", "created_at": "2026-10-03T15:27:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2106405664688046574"], "id": "2106405664688046574", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Gemini 4 Argon is #1 on Mercor's APEX-SWE for building systems that connect several services, at 72.5%.\n\nOn debugging production failures from logs, it scores 26.8%.\n\nReading more doesn't help, its passing debug runs use about as many tokens as the failing ones.\n\nGrading combines https://t.co/hkYBxMg2Ju", "url": "https://x.com/alcreon/status/2106405664688046574"}, {"author_id": "1445377133547765763", "created_at": "2026-10-14T14:19:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2110374901680837110"], "id": "2110374901680837110", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 15, "impression_count": 1951, "like_count": 38, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "\ud835\uddda\ud835\uddf2\ud835\uddfa\ud835\uddf6\ud835\uddfb\ud835\uddf6 \ud835\udff0 \ud835\uddd4\ud835\uddff\ud835\uddf4\ud835\uddfc\ud835\uddfb \ud835\ude03\ud835\ude00. \ud835\uddd4\ud835\uddfb\ud835