eply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2109744804410392831", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "A 1M-token output limit is wild. I\u2019d love to see what Gemini 4 Argon can actually build or debug in a single run. Are there demos of the software engineering workflows? Until then this cartoon is surprisingly accurate! https://t.co/fBO9JPzAUl", "url": "https://x.com/ncsuian/status/2109794814820749665"}, {"author_id": "1555483928022097920", "created_at": "2026-10-03T18:58:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2106458899012300927"], "id": "2106458899012300927", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 127, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "GEMINI 4 ARGON IS OPTIMIZING ITS OWN HARDWARE INFRASTRUCTURE\n\nGoogle just revealed that Gemini 4 Argon agents are actively profiling and refactoring internal systems at unprecedented scale.\n\nBy analyzing fleet-wide telemetry, Argon identified low-level bottlenecks and https://t.co/yezywxbH1i", "url": "https://x.com/noxflux/status/2106458899012300927"}, {"author_id": "2067188544700063744", "created_at": "2026-10-07T09:00:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2107757954988638694"], "id": "2107757954988638694", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 147, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\ud83d\udea8Gemini 4 Argon just quietly hit Google Cloud.\n\nIf history holds, the official launch drops the exact same day. With a massive 1M output token limit, this model is engineered to refactor entire codebases in a single pass.\n\nWhat are you testing first?", "url": "https://x.com/syncshiftstudio/status/2107757954988638694"}, {"author_id": "1531527487561375744", "created_at": "2026-10-06T17:41:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2107526630566461785"], "id": "2107526630566461785", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1531527487561375744", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2107526376807161997", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "\ud83d\udcac 3/3: Where Argon shines\n\u200bGemini 4 Argon excels at:\n\u2705 Multi-file codebase refactoring (DeepSWE)\n\u2705 Complex legal, financial &amp; long-context analysis\n\u2705 Defensive cybersecurity &amp; bug hunting (CWE-bench)\n\u200bGradual rollout has started for API users. Is this enough to make you", "url": "https://x.com/Stacki_TV/status/2107526630566461785"}, {"author_id": "1326885552793247751", "created_at": "2026-10-06T10:42:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2107421297949233245"], "id": "2107421297949233245", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 12, "impression_count": 7139, "like_count": 144, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "Gemini 4 Argon update:\n\nGoogle engineers are using Argon for:\n\n\u2192 debugging\n\u2192 large-scale codebase migrations\n\u2192 algorithm design\n\u2192 quantum research\n\u2192 data-center memory optimization\n\nAnd this is happening while reports still question its real-world coding consistency.", "url": "https://x.com/StatsWire/status/2107421297949233245"}, {"author_id": "2094446774169567232", "created_at": "2026-10-05T14:23:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2107114579696230450"], "id": "2107114579696230450", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1895205185250828292", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 50, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2107074897101136237", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kapilansh_twt Wake me up when Gemini 4 Argon can actually debug a C++ memory leak without apologizing and hallucinating a non-existent library. The 'AI race' is just a multi-billion dollar marketing marathon.", "url": "https://x.com/KazanVisual/status/2107114579696230450"}, {"author_id": "2088308682065154048", "created_at": "2026-10-14T06:02:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2110249744820027592"], "id": "2110249744820027592", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 139, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "6 ways to use Gemini 4 Argon without a Google AI Ultra subscription:\n\nGemini Web App\n    Google AI Pro subscribers can access Gemini 4 Argon through the Gemini app, even if it\u2019s unavailable to them in Antigravity.\nGoogle AI Studio\n    Access Gemini 4 Argon through Google\u2019s API https://t.co/Q6RBHNFp4v", "url": "https://x.com/trywavecode/status/2110249744820027592"}, {"author_id": "2002214728983326721", "created_at": "2026-10-14T01:10:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2110176453782577597"], "id": "2110176453782577597", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 133, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2110114439227724041", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Gemini 4 Argon is live for developers \ud83e\udd16\n\nBuilt for tough, multi-step real-world work \u2699\ufe0f\nIt handles up to 1M tokens of text and media at once.\nYou can load an entire code repo or hundreds of contract pages in one prompt.\nGreat for code refactoring, AI agents, security testing, https://t.co/HQXxNAqPwE https://t.co/A514xOyGPz", "url": "https://x.com/PolyokeyMoney/status/2110176453782577597"}, {"author_id": "1177957753295425536", "created_at": "2026-10-05T17:02:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2107154434212188286"], "id": "2107154434212188286", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 503, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Anyone using Gemini 4 Argon for real-world coding or long-horizon tasks?\n\nHow\u2019s the performance so far compared to Claude / GPT \u2014 especially for large codebases, debugging, and architecture?\n\nWould love to hear some real developer feedback. \ud83d\udc40\n\n#Gemini #Gemini4 #AI #AICoding", "url": "https://x.com/JalondharaVivek/status/2107154434212188286"}, {"author_id": "1871946053223587840", "created_at": "2026-10-03T15:32:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2106406947737989153"], "id": "2106406947737989153", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 117, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Google has launched Gemini 4 Argon, a new flagship AI model designed to push deeper into software engineering, advanced reasoning, and cybersecurity work.\n\nThe model is positioned for longer-running technical tasks, including complex coding workflows, debugging, system analysis, https://t.co/RJyl7bo1oS", "url": "https://x.com/techamericaofcl/status/2106406947737989153"}, {"author_id": "1971726739933220865", "created_at": "2026-10-04T22:34:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2106875716797354082"], "id": "2106875716797354082", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 105, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Google's Gemini 4 Argon is pushing AI toward long-running engineering and cybersecurity tasks.\n\nThe bigger shift isn't just smarter answers.\n\nIt's agents that can plan, code, test, debug and iterate through complex work.\n\nAI is becoming an engineering worker.", "url": "https://x.com/theazeeztech/status/2106875716797354082"}, {"author_id": "2065713304560189440", "created_at": "2026-10-02T12:22:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2105996889988690144"], "id": "2105996889988690144", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2065713304560189440", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 43, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2105996887618916688", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "5/6 Workload Fit:\n- Massive repo refactoring and cyber defense: Evaluate Gemini 4 Argon\n- Nuanced documentation, structured coding, and MCP agents: Evaluate Claude Sonnet 5.5 / Opus 5.5\n- High-volume APIs, tiered routing, and Microsoft/Azure stacks: Evaluate OpenAI GPT-6", "url": "https://x.com/techniqco/status/2105996889988690144"}, {"author_id": "1372421378", "created_at": "2026-10-09T16:40:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2108598460157227390"], "id": "2108598460157227390", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2098766407920205824", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2108586457644560652", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ashawv5i Interesting find! A merged PR mentioning Gemini 4 Argon is exciting, but not proof of a release. I'm curious to see how it performs in real-world coding, complex debugging, and agentic workflows. Waiting for official benchmarks!", "url": "https://x.com/NaveedTechLab/status/2108598460157227390"}, {"author_id": "750013974570078208", "created_at": "2026-10-14T20:47:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2110472677366374846"], "id": "2110472677366374846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 99, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Gemini 4 Argon Is Here And Cheap\nAfter months trailing rivals, Google has opened Gemini 4 Argon to paying users at roughly a fifth of its rivals' per-token price. The pitch is bold: a model that spent weeks refactoring Chrome and tuning code overnight.\n\nhttps://t.co/6eqcCPPPzP https://t.co/cADXNC4UAV", "url": "https://x.com/5alhi/status/2110472677366374846"}, {"author_id": "2108095257380335616", "created_at": "2026-10-14T12:30:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2110347580387254307"], "id": "2110347580387254307", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Gemini 4 Argon is live on the paid Gemini API.\n\n- ID: gemini-4-argon\n- Intro $2/$10 per 1M (\u2192 $4/$20 Dec